From: Vahiru <nekovahiru@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sc8280xp-huawei-gaokun3: drop FIXME comment on rear camera 180-degree rotation

The rear OV13B10 sensor's rotation = <180> property has been verified on
hardware with libcamera and the Android Camera HAL. Update the comment in
sc8280xp-huawei-gaokun3-camera.dtsi accordingly.

Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-huawei-gaokun3-camera.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-huawei-gaokun3-camera.dtsi
@@ -226,7 +226,9 @@
 		lens-focus = <&voice_coil_motor>;
 
 		orientation = <1>;
-		rotation = <180>; /* FIXME */
+		/* Counter-clockwise (video-interface-devices.yaml). Confirmed on
+		 * device 2026-09-24: preview upright, SENSOR_ORIENTATION 180. */
+		rotation = <180>;
 
 		port {
 			ov13b10_ep: endpoint {
